{title: Christ Is Our Cornerstone}
{artist: John Chandler, C. Michael Pilato}
{key: D}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: 88}

Verse 1
[D]Christ is our cornerstone.
On [Bm]Him alone [A]we [D]build.
With His true [G]saints alone,
[Bm]The [G]courts of [A]heav'n are [D]filled.
On [G]His great [D]love, our [A]hopes we [Bm]place.
Of [G]joys above [Bm]and [Asus]present [A]grace.
Christ [D]is our cornerstone.
[Bm]We [Gmaj7]build on [A]Him alone.

Verse 2
Here gracious God draw near,
As in your name we bow.
Each true petition hear;
Accept each faithful vow.
And more and more [Gmaj7]on all who pray
Your blessings pour each holy day.
Christ [G]is our cornerstone.
We build on Him alone.

Verse 3
Jesus is our [A]firm foundation,
[D/F#]Precious [G]stone at [A]God's right [D]hand.
[D/F#]He's the [G]Rock of [A]our [N.C.]Salvation,
[Bm]And [A/C#]the [D]gates of Hell won't [Asus]stand.

Verse 4
[A]Here may we gain from heav'n,
The grace which we implore.
And may that grace once giv'n
Be with us evermore.
Until that day when all the blessed
Are called away to endless rest.
Christ [D]is our cornerstone.
[Bm]We [Gmaj7]build on [A]Him alone.
[Bm]We [Gmaj7]build on [A]Him alone.
